  "claim_ceiling": "Passing establishes only that, on the frozen four-G panel, a fixed F-plus-structural-G-plus-closure carrier and four fixed public recurrent stage rows can be advanced to the tested semantic boundary by forwarding four public target label tokens per G variant and replacing only their attention positions. The prospectively charged candidate source law is 130 + 4N tokens, 146 tokens at N=4, versus 209 + 27N for the predecessor and 79 + 51N for active-F branching; its asymptotic variable-source ratio is 4/130. Full-logit parity is diagnostic rather than expected. The fixed stage rows and full active cache allocation are counted. This does not establish a direct label-group operator, context-independent update, numerical recursive fidelity, inverse restoration, bounded whole-process cost with depth, vanishing fresh-work ratio by itself, catalytic recurrence, Small Wall crossing, or unbounded inference."
